{"title":"2022 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 16","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A standard fair coin is tossed three times. What is the probability that the three outcomes are all the same?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/a/e8ad39939e8d9c8fa896c54fa8834162357a4185.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ \\frac{1}{2} \\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ \\frac{3}{16} \\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ \\frac{1}{4} \\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ \\frac{5}{16} \\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ \\frac{1}{8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"389\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_1_.28Modified_from_Official_Solution.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1_(Modified_from_Official_Solution)\">Solution 1 (Modified from Official Solution)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1 (Modified from Official Solution)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>There would be a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/6/b76a0cdaf0402eb3b8e6bc72f8cb9bfa03c7b583.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(\\frac{1}{2})^{3} = \\frac{1}{8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"74\" height=\"38\" /> probability of having all heads in three flips, and the same probability for having all tails in three flips. \n</p><p>The probability of having all the same outcome in three flips would then be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/1/5417712ccfc3875e5e42caa4ace3d1f0a2413c14.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{8} + \\frac{1}{8} = \\frac{1 + 1}{8} = \\frac{2}{8} = \\boxed {\\textbf {(C) } \\frac{1}{4}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"240\" height=\"49\" /> probability.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher and CEMC\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For all three outcomes to be the same, the last two must be the same as the first one. This would have a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/c/75c598625943f7073b013d78fb4a6dadef70e168.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(\\frac{1}{2})^{2} = \\boxed {\\textbf {(C) } \\frac{1}{4}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"120\" height=\"49\" /> probability of happening.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher \n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)\" title=\"2022 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7)\">2022 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7)</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2022 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2022 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a hre